────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2. THE EMBEDDED DATA — NOT MIT
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

public_html/index.html and skydata.js contain three packed strings —
STAR_BLOB, STAR_NAMES and CON_BLOB — that are not covered by the MIT grant
above. They are derived from other people's work and keep their licences. The same
goes for every image in public_html/tex/.

STAR_BLOB, STAR_NAMES
  An extract of the HYG database v3.8 (1,637 stars to magnitude 5: right
  ascension, declination, visual magnitude, colour index, proper names),
  by David Nash / astronexus — https://github.com/astronexus/HYG-Database

  Licensed CC BY-SA 4.0. https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

  This extract is Adapted Material. If you redistribute it, modified or
  not, you must attribute the HYG database and license the extract under
  CC BY-SA 4.0 or a compatible licence. You may not add restrictions to it.
  build-skydata.js regenerates it from the upstream CSV.

public_html/tex/{io,europa,ganymede,callisto,titan,enceladus,dione,rhea,
                 iapetus,triton,phobos}.jpg
  Controlled global mosaics from the USGS Astrogeology Science Center,
  derived from NASA Voyager, Galileo, Cassini, New Horizons and Viking
  imagery -- https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/ -- downscaled to 1024x512.

  Public domain (US Government work). No restrictions; credit is given in
  the page's About panel as a courtesy.

public_html/tex/{mercury,venus,earth,mars,jupiter,saturn,uranus,neptune,moon}.jpg
  Planetary and lunar surface maps from Solar System Scope --
  https://www.solarsystemscope.com/textures/ -- downscaled to 1024x512 and
  recompressed. Built from Messenger, Viking, Cassini and Hubble imagery.

  Licensed CC BY 4.0. https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Attribution required; credit is given in the page's About panel.

