────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
3. NOT LICENSED HERE
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The planetary elements are from "Approximate Positions of the Major
Planets" by E. M. Standish, JPL Solar System Dynamics; the rotational
elements are from the IAU Working Group on Cartographic Coordinates and
Rotational Elements 2015 report — a published table
of physical constants, reproduced as fact. The lunar series is Paul
Schlyter's abridged theory, likewise. Neither claims a licence over the
numbers, and none is asserted here.

The page loads Outfit and DM Sans from Google Fonts; both are SIL Open
Font License 1.1 and are not redistributed in this repository.
